//  Why an explicit ruling and not "same stale reason, lift it": with G21+G16 open, opening this line means
//  that ~100 passes after wb_serve starts the relay closes AND, MotorPowerOnDelay (=4) seconds later,
//  CountMotorPowerDelay RELEASES the arm-Z / cassette brakes -- with nobody having pressed anything.  golden
//  can afford that because its start-up InitMotor has servo-ONed every axis; in this tree the golden motor
//  objects never open a 1203 axis (uiDevhand==0), so nothing here guarantees the Z drives are servo-ON when
//  the brakes open.  Whether EastSun's drives hold Z by themselves is exactly what needs his answer.
//AI(W906-MT-FIX1) 20260926: GATE G31a LIFTED -- golden :4116 verbatim.  EastSun ruling 20260926: "照舊版打開" (automatic
//  motor power-on ~100 DoSystem passes after start-up, golden's 1 s busy loop included).  The hazard in the note above --
//  CountMotorPowerDelay releasing the arm-Z / cassette brakes MotorPowerOnDelay seconds later with no drive servo-ON --
//  is covered by the same ruling's servo-ON check on every release (W906_BrakeReleaseOK in G16 / G05 / HOME): a group
//  whose 1203 axes are not servo-ON keeps its brake held.
            DoMotorPowerOn();
            SW[SwServerON].On();
            #ifdef SOFT_SIMULTE
                MotorPowerOnDelay=0;
            #else
                MotorPowerOnDelay=SERVER_MOTOR_POWER_ON_DELAY;
            #endif
            bMotorPowerState=true;
            flag=false;
            MOTPower=true;
//            fMain->palMain->Enabled=true;
//AI(W906-PT-csystem-g2) 20260809: GATE G30 -- golden csystem.cpp:4127-4128.  fMain->SitePanel is NOT a member of the
// ported TfMain (tree-wide grep for `SitePanel` = zero hits).  DEFAULT: nothing.
// BEHAVIOUR DELTA: the site-panel Visible=false/true repaint kick after the first motor
